  "question": {
    "html": "<p>Light with photons of energy 8.0 × 10<sup>−20 </sup>J are incident on a metal surface in a photoelectric experiment.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p>\n<p>The work function of the metal surface is 4.8 × 10<sup>−20 </sup>J . What minimum voltage is required for the ammeter reading to fall to zero?</p>\n<p>[1]</p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\">0.2 V</li><li data-label=\"B\">0.3 V</li><li data-label=\"C\">0.5 V</li><li data-label=\"D\">0.8 V</li></ol>"
  },
